-- coa15-ch1.l4: Part 18 (Acquisition by limited company of its own shares), Chapter 1 (General provisions), ss 658 to 676
-- (lines 8745-8930 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rules of 2026-10-29 and 2026-11-05; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the term, or the consequence follows.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a condition the text introduces with "if", "where",
--               "when", "unless", "until" or "only", a period the text fixes in its own words, a flat negative.
--               Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: it lists without closing the list, says "includes", leaves a term undefined, is
--               silent, points outside the sources, or limits a grant or prohibition by a scope the text names.
--               Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Seam inputs (answers of other parts) are MAYBE BOOLEAN and pass NOTHING through.

