-- ---- s 658: the general rule ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:8749 | (1) A limited company must not acquire its own shares, whether by purchase, subscription or otherwise, except in accordance with the provisions of this Part.
@ref s 658(1) General rule against limited company acquiring its own shares (src:8749-8749)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquisition is in accordance with the provisions of Part 18` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(1) a limited company must not make the acquisition` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A limited company must not acquire its own shares"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the acquisition is in accordance with the provisions of Part 18`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in accordance with the provisions of this Part"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the acquisition is in accordance with the Part is the other provisions of the Part, which the caller answers

DECLARE `s 658(1) act of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 658(1) acquire its own shares, whether by purchase, subscription or otherwise`

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: no WITHIN, because the text states no period (a SHANT with a WITHIN sunsets).
@ref s 658(1) General rule against limited company acquiring its own shares (src:8749-8749)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 658(1) act of the company`
`s 658(1) the limited company shant acquire its own shares` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 658(1) acquire its own shares, whether by purchase, subscription or otherwise`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 658(1): a limited company acquired its own shares otherwise than in accordance with Part 18"

-- src:8750 | (2) If a company purports to act in contravention of this section—
-- src:8751 | (a) an offence is committed by—
-- src:8752 | (i) the company, and
-- src:8753 | (ii) every officer of the company who is in default, and
@ref s 658(2)(a) Offence by the company and every officer in default (src:8750-8753)
GIVEN `the company purports to act in contravention of section 658` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(2)(a) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company purports to act in contravention of section 658`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company purports to act in contravention of this section"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by the company and every officer in default

-- src:8754 | (b) the purported acquisition is void.
@ref s 658(2)(b) The purported acquisition is void (src:8754-8754)
GIVEN `the company purports to act in contravention of section 658` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(2)(b) the purported acquisition is void` MEANS
    IF `the company purports to act in contravention of section 658`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company purports to act in contravention of this section"

-- src:8755 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:8756 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:8757 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:8758 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:8759 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 658(3) Penalty (src:8755-8759)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 658(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives the penalty on indictment and on summary conviction by place; a summary conviction with no place named is not a case it states

