GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are acquired for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 659(1) a limited company may acquire its own shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are fully paid` AND (NOT `the shares are acquired for valuable consideration`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of its own fully paid shares otherwise than for valuable consideration"

DECLARE `s 659(2) kind of acquisition` IS ONE OF
    `s 659(2)(a) an acquisition of shares in a reduction of capital duly made`
    `s 659(2)(b)(i) a purchase in pursuance of an order of the court under section 98`
    `s 659(2)(b)(ii) a purchase in pursuance of an order of the court under section 721(6)`
    `s 659(2)(b)(iii) a purchase in pursuance of an order of the court under section 759`
    `s 659(2)(b)(iv) a purchase in pursuance of an order of the court under Part 30`
    `s 659(2)(c) a forfeiture of shares, or acceptance of shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the articles, for failure to pay a sum payable in respect of the shares`
    `s 659(2) any other acquisition`

-- src:8762 | (2) Section 658 does not prohibit—
-- src:8763 | (a) the acquisition of shares in a reduction of capital duly made;
-- src:8764 | (b) the purchase of shares in pursuance of an order of the court under—
-- src:8765 | (i) section 98 (application to court to cancel resolution for re-registration as a private company),
-- src:8766 | (ii) section 721(6) (powers of court on objection to redemption or purchase of shares out of capital),
-- src:8767 | (iii) section 759 (remedial order in case of breach of prohibition of public offers by private company), or
-- src:8768 | (iv) Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice);
-- src:8769 | (c) the forfeiture of shares, or the acceptance of shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the company's articles, for failure to pay any sum payable in respect of the shares.
@ref s 659(2) Section 658 does not prohibit (src:8762-8769)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 659(2) kind of acquisition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 659(2) section 658 does not prohibit the acquisition` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 659(2) any other acquisition` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Section 658 does not prohibit—" lists three cases and does not close the list with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

