`s 661(4)(b) the court has the power to relieve him` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-661-4b: "the court has the same power to relieve him" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    CONSIDER `s 661(4)(a) the subscriber or director may apply to the court for relief`
              `he is a subscriber to the company's memorandum or a director of the company`
              `he has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made for the recovery of any such amount from him`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` TRUE
              `the subscriber or director has acted honestly and reasonably`
              `having regard to all the circumstances of the case, he ought fairly to be relieved from liability`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a subscriber to a company's memorandum or a director of a company has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Chapter 1: Shares held by or for a public company, ss 662 to 669
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:8803 | (1) This section applies in the case of a public company—
-- src:8804 | (a) where shares in the company are forfeited, or surrendered to the company in lieu of forfeiture, in pursuance of the articles, for failure to pay any sum payable in respect of the shares;
-- src:8805 | (b) where shares in the company are surrendered to the company in pursuance of section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986 (c. 53);
-- src:8806 | (c) where shares in the company are acquired by it (otherwise than in accordance with this Part or Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)) and the company has a beneficial interest in the shares;
-- src:8807 | (d) where a nominee of the company acquires shares in the company from a third party without financial assistance being given directly or indirectly by the company and the company has a beneficial interest in the shares; or
-- src:8808 | (e) where a person acquires shares in the company, with financial assistance given to him, directly or indirectly, by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition, and the company has a beneficial interest in the shares.
@ref s 662(1) Duty to cancel shares in a public company held by or for the company: when the section applies (src:8803-8808)
DECLARE `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` IS ONE OF
    `s 662(1)(a) forfeited, or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture, in pursuance of the articles, for failure to pay a sum payable in respect of the shares`
    `s 662(1)(b) surrendered to the company in pursuance of section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986`
    `s 662(1)(c) acquired by the company otherwise than in accordance with Part 18 or Part 30`
    `s 662(1)(d) acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance given by the company`
    `s 662(1)(e) acquired by a person with financial assistance given to him by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition`
    `s 662(1) in another way`

DECLARE `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company` HAS
    `s 662(1) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` IS A `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held`
    `s 662(1)(c) to (e) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 662(2) the shares or any interest of the company in them have been previously disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 662(2)(b) the cancellation brings the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 662(1) Duty to cancel shares in a public company held by or for the company: when the section applies (src:8803-8808)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(1) this section applies to the shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT held's `s 662(1) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in the case of a public company"
    ELSE CONSIDER held's `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held`
         WHEN `s 662(1)(a) forfeited, or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture, in pursuance of the articles, for failure to pay a sum payable in respect of the shares` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 662(1)(b) surrendered to the company in pursuance of section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 662(1) in another way` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a public company— (a) where ... (b) where ... (c) where ... (d) where ... (e) where"
         OTHERWISE
              IF held's `s 662(1)(c) to (e) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the company has a beneficial interest in the shares"

-- src:8809 | (2) Unless the shares or any interest of the company in them are previously disposed of, the company must—
-- src:8810 | (a) cancel the shares and diminish the amount of the company's share capital by the nominal value of the shares cancelled, and
@ref s 662(2)(a) Unless previously disposed of, the company must cancel the shares and diminish its share capital (src:8809-8810)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(2)(a) the company must cancel the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 662(1) this section applies to the shares` held
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF held's `s 662(2) the shares or any interest of the company in them have been previously disposed of`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the shares or any interest of the company in them are previously disposed of"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a public company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in the case of a public company"

-- src:8811 | (b) where the effect is that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is brought below the authorised minimum, apply for re-registration as a private company, stating the effect of the cancellation.
@ref s 662(2)(b) Where the cancellation brings the allotted share capital below the authorised minimum, the company must apply for re-registration (src:8811-8811)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(2)(b) the company must apply for re-registration as a private company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 662(2)(a) the company must cancel the shares` held
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF held's `s 662(2)(b) the cancellation brings the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the effect is that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is brought below the authorised minimum"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the shares or any interest of the company in them are previously disposed of, the company must"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in the case of a public company"

-- src:8812 | (3) It must do so no later than—
-- src:8813 | (a) in a case within subsection (1)(a) or (b), three years from the date of the forfeiture or surrender;
-- src:8814 | (b) in a case within subsection (1)(c) or (d), three years from the date of the acquisition;
-- src:8815 | (c) in a case within subsection (1)(e), one year from the date of the acquisition.
@ref s 662(3) It must do so no later than three years (or one year) from the date (src:8812-8815)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
      `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 662(3) the last day for cancelling the shares and for applying for re-registration` MEANS
    CONSIDER held's `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held`
    WHEN `s 662(1)(a) forfeited, or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture, in pursuance of the articles, for failure to pay a sum payable in respect of the shares` THEN JUST (`add years` `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` 3)
    WHEN `s 662(1)(b) surrendered to the company in pursuance of section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986` THEN JUST (`add years` `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` 3)
    WHEN `s 662(1)(c) acquired by the company otherwise than in accordance with Part 18 or Part 30` THEN JUST (`add years` `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` 3)
    WHEN `s 662(1)(d) acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance given by the company` THEN JUST (`add years` `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` 3)
    WHEN `s 662(1)(e) acquired by a person with financial assistance given to him by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition` THEN JUST (`add years` `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` 1)
    WHEN `s 662(1) in another way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) states a period for the cases within subsection (1)(a) to (e) only

@ref s 662(3) It must do so no later than three years (or one year) from the date (src:8812-8815)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
      `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company cancelled the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(3) the company cancelled the shares in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 662(3) the last day for cancelling the shares and for applying for re-registration` held `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition`
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN
         IF `the date on which the company cancelled the shares` AT MOST lastday
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must do so no later than— ... three years from the date ... one year from the date"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) states a period for the cases within subsection (1)(a) to (e) only

-- The duty of s 662(2)(a) with the period of s 662(3), as a regulative rule: the clock starts on the date of the event
-- and the last day is the date s 662(3) fixes. The days are counted between the two dates.
-- src:8809 | (2) Unless the shares or any interest of the company in them are previously disposed of, the company must—
-- src:8810 | (a) cancel the shares and diminish the amount of the company's share capital by the nominal value of the shares cancelled, and
-- src:8811 | (b) where the effect is that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is brought below the authorised minimum, apply for re-registration as a private company, stating the effect of the cancellation.
-- src:8812 | (3) It must do so no later than—
-- src:8813 | (a) in a case within subsection (1)(a) or (b), three years from the date of the forfeiture or surrender;
-- src:8814 | (b) in a case within subsection (1)(c) or (d), three years from the date of the acquisition;
-- src:8815 | (c) in a case within subsection (1)(e), one year from the date of the acquisition.
@ref s 662(2)(a) and (3) Duty to cancel the shares by the last day (src:8809-8815)
GIVEN `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` IS A DATE
      `the last day for cancelling the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 661(4) act in Chapter 1`
`s 662(2)(a) the company must cancel the shares by the last day` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 662(2)(a) cancel the shares and diminish the amount of the company's share capital by the nominal value of the shares cancelled`
    WITHIN (Day `the last day for cancelling the shares` MINUS Day `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 662(2)(a), (3): the shares were not cancelled by the last day"

-- src:8811 | (b) where the effect is that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is brought below the authorised minimum, apply for re-registration as a private company, stating the effect of the cancellation.
-- src:8812 | (3) It must do so no later than—
-- src:8813 | (a) in a case within subsection (1)(a) or (b), three years from the date of the forfeiture or surrender;
-- src:8814 | (b) in a case within subsection (1)(c) or (d), three years from the date of the acquisition;
-- src:8815 | (c) in a case within subsection (1)(e), one year from the date of the acquisition.
@ref s 662(2)(b) and (3) Duty to apply for re-registration by the last day (src:8811-8815)
GIVEN `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` IS A DATE
      `the last day for applying for re-registration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 661(4) act in Chapter 1`
`s 662(2)(b) the company must apply for re-registration as a private company by the last day` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 662(2)(b) apply for re-registration as a private company, stating the effect of the cancellation`
    WITHIN (Day `the last day for applying for re-registration` MINUS Day `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 662(2)(b), (3): the company did not apply for re-registration by the last day"

-- src:8816 | (4) The directors of the company may take any steps necessary to enable the company to comply with this section, and may do so without complying with the provisions of Chapter 10 of Part 17 (reduction of capital).
@ref s 662(4) The directors may take any steps necessary, without complying with Chapter 10 of Part 17 (src:8816-8816)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(4) the directors may take the steps without complying with Chapter 10 of Part 17` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 662(1) this section applies to the shares` held
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may take any steps necessary to enable the company to comply with this section"

DECLARE `s 662(5) who would exercise the voting rights` IS ONE OF
    `s 662(5) the company`
    `s 662(5) the nominee or other shareholder`

-- src:8818 | (5) Neither the company nor, in a case within subsection (1)(d) or (e), the nominee or other shareholder may exercise any voting rights in respect of the shares.
@ref s 662(5) Neither the company nor, in a case within (1)(d) or (e), the nominee or other shareholder may exercise any voting rights (src:8818-8818)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
      who IS A `s 662(5) who would exercise the voting rights`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(5) the person may exercise voting rights in respect of the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 662(1) this section applies to the shares` held
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         CONSIDER who
         WHEN `s 662(5) the company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Neither the company ... may exercise any voting rights in respect of the shares"
         WHEN `s 662(5) the nominee or other shareholder` THEN
              CONSIDER held's `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held`
              WHEN `s 662(1)(d) acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance given by the company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (1)(d) or (e), the nominee or other shareholder may [not] exercise any voting rights"
              WHEN `s 662(1)(e) acquired by a person with financial assistance given to him by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (1)(d) or (e), the nominee or other shareholder may [not] exercise any voting rights"
              OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case within subsection (1)(d) or (e)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in the case of a public company"

-- src:8819 | (6) Any purported exercise of those rights is void.
@ref s 662(6) Any purported exercise of those rights is void (src:8819-8819)
GIVEN held IS A `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company`
      who IS A `s 662(5) who would exercise the voting rights`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(6) the purported exercise of the voting rights is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 662(5) the person may exercise voting rights in respect of the shares` held who
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any purported exercise of those rights is void": "those rights" are the rights subsection (5) bars

-- src:8821 | (1) Where a company cancels shares in order to comply with section 662, it must within one month after the shares are cancelled give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares cancelled.
@ref s 663(1) Notice of cancellation of shares: within one month after the shares are cancelled (src:8821-8821)
GIVEN `the date on which the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 663(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` MEANS `add months` `the date on which the shares were cancelled` 1
-- fork F-month: "within one month after" is read as the corresponding date one month on (clamped to the month's last day); the other reading ends on the day before it

@ref s 663(1) Notice of cancellation of shares: within one month after the shares are cancelled (src:8821-8821)
GIVEN `the date on which the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 663(1) the notice was given within one month after the shares were cancelled` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the shares were cancelled`
       AND `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar` AT MOST (`s 663(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` `the date on which the shares were cancelled`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month after the shares are cancelled give notice to the registrar"

@ref s 663(1) Notice of cancellation of shares: within one month after the shares are cancelled (src:8821-8821)
GIVEN `the date on which the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 661(4) act in Chapter 1`
`s 663(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 663(1) give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares cancelled`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 663(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` `the date on which the shares were cancelled`) MINUS Day `the date on which the shares were cancelled`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 663(1): notice of the cancellation was not given to the registrar within one month after the shares were cancelled"

-- src:8822 | (2) The notice must be accompanied by a statement of capital.
@ref s 663(2) The notice must be accompanied by a statement of capital (src:8822-8822)
GIVEN `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 663(2) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` MEANS
    IF `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be accompanied by a statement of capital." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8823 | (3) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital immediately following the cancellation—
-- src:8824 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:8825 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:8826 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:8827 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:8828 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:8829 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:8830 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
-- src:8831 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 663(3) The statement of capital must state (src:8823-8831)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 663(3) statement of capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 663(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` MEANS
    -- fork F-empty-list: with no class entry in the facts the answer is NOTHING: the facts do not say that the company has a class of shares
    IF (NOT statement's `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the company`)
       OR (NOT statement's `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`)
       OR (NOT statement's `s 663(3) states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of capital must state ... (a) the total number of shares of the company, (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares, (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
    ELSE CONSIDER statement's `s 663(3) entries for the classes of shares`
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the facts give no class entry, so they do not say whether the company has a class of shares for which (c) requires one
         WHEN entry FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
              IF `s 663(3)(c) every entry states what paragraph (c) requires` (entry FOLLOWED BY rest)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) for each class of shares— (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares, (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

@ref s 663(3)(c) The statement of capital must state, for each class of shares, three items (src:8827-8830)
GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `s 663(3) class entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 663(3)(c) every entry states what paragraph (c) requires` MEANS
    all (GIVEN e YIELD (e's `s 663(3) states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares of the class`)
                       AND (e's `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the class`)
                       AND (e's `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of the class`)) entries

-- src:8832 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:8833 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8834 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 663(4) Offence (src:8832-8834)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 663` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 663(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `default is made in complying with section 663`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:8835 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 663(5) Penalty (src:8835-8835)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 663(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states the penalty on summary conviction only
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF how, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- ---- s 664: re-registration as a private company in consequence of cancellation ------------------------

-- src:8837 | (1) Where a company is obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662, the directors may resolve that the company should be so re-registered.
@ref s 664(1) Where a company is obliged to re-register as a private company, the directors may resolve (src:8837-8837)
GIVEN `the company is obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(1) the directors may resolve that the company should be re-registered as a private company` MEANS
    IF `the company is obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662, the directors may resolve"

@ref s 664(1) The directors may resolve that the company should be re-registered (src:8837-8837)
GIVEN who IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 661(4) act in Chapter 1`
`s 664(1) the directors may resolve to re-register` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MAY `s 664(1) resolve that the company should be re-registered as a private company`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:8838 | Chapter 3 of Part 3 (resolutions affecting a company's constitution) applies to any such resolution.
@ref s 664(1) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to any such resolution (src:8838-8838)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 664(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(1) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 664(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to any such resolution"

-- src:8839 | (2) The resolution may make such changes—
-- src:8840 | (a) in the company's name, and
-- src:8841 | (b) in the company's articles,
-- src:8842 | as are necessary in connection with its becoming a private company.
@ref s 664(2) The resolution may make such changes in the name and the articles as are necessary (src:8839-8842)
GIVEN `the change is to the company's name or to its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is necessary in connection with the company's becoming a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(2) the resolution may make the change` MEANS
    IF `the change is to the company's name or to its articles`
       AND `the change is necessary in connection with the company's becoming a private company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such changes— (a) in the company's name, and (b) in the company's articles, as are necessary in connection with its becoming a private company"

-- src:8843 | (3) The application for re-registration must contain a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration.
@ref s 664(3) The application for re-registration must contain a statement of the proposed name (src:8843-8843)
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(3) the application contains what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application for re-registration must contain a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8844 | (4) The application must be accompanied by—
-- src:8845 | (a) a copy of the resolution (unless a copy has already been forwarded under Chapter 3 of Part 3),
-- src:8846 | (b) a copy of the company's articles as amended by the resolution, and
-- src:8847 | (c) a statement of compliance.
@ref s 664(4) The application must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution, the amended articles and a statement of compliance (src:8844-8847)
GIVEN `a copy of the resolution accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the resolution has already been forwarded under Chapter 3 of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the company's articles as amended by the resolution accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of compliance accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(4) the application is accompanied as the section requires` MEANS
    IF (`a copy of the resolution accompanies the application` OR `a copy of the resolution has already been forwarded under Chapter 3 of Part 3`)
       AND `a copy of the company's articles as amended by the resolution accompanies the application`
       AND `a statement of compliance accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be accompanied by— (a) a copy of the resolution (unless a copy has already been forwarded under Chapter 3 of Part 3), (b) ..., and (c) a statement of compliance." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8848 | (5) The statement of compliance required is a statement that the requirements of this section as to re-registration as a private company have been complied with.
@ref s 664(5) The statement of compliance required is a statement that the requirements of this section have been complied with (src:8848-8848)
GIVEN `the statement says that the requirements of section 664 as to re-registration as a private company have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(5) the statement is the statement of compliance required` MEANS
    IF `the statement says that the requirements of section 664 as to re-registration as a private company have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance required is a statement that the requirements of this section as to re-registration as a private company have been complied with."

-- src:8849 | (6) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private company.
@ref s 664(6) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence (src:8849-8849)
GIVEN `the statement is the statement of compliance required by section 664(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664(6) the registrar may accept the statement as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the statement is the statement of compliance required by section 664(5)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence": the grant is limited to the statement of compliance

-- ---- s 665: issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration -----------------------------------

-- src:8851 | (1) If on an application under section 664 the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private company, the company shall be re-registered accordingly.
@ref s 665(1) If the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled, the company shall be re-registered (src:8851-8851)
GIVEN `on an application under section 664 the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 665(1) the company shall be re-registered as a private company` MEANS
    IF `on an application under section 664 the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under section 664 the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private company, the company shall be re-registered accordingly."

-- src:8852 | (2) The registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 665(2) The registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case (src:8852-8852)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 661(4) act in Chapter 1`
`s 665(2) the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 665(2) issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "s 665(2): the registrar did not issue the certificate"

-- src:8853 | (3) The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued.
@ref s 665(3) The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued (src:8853-8853)
GIVEN `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 665(3) the certificate states what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` AND `the certificate states the date on which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8854 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:8855 | (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a private company, and
@ref s 665(4)(a) On the issue of the certificate the company becomes a private company (src:8854-8855)
GIVEN `the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 665(4)(a) the company becomes a private company by virtue of the issue of the certificate` MEANS
    IF `the certificate has been issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a private company"

-- src:8856 | (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect.
@ref s 665(4)(b) On the issue of the certificate the changes in the company's name and articles take effect (src:8856-8856)
GIVEN `the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 665(4)(b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect` MEANS
    IF `the certificate has been issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect."

-- src:8857 | (5) The certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act as to re-registration have been complied with.
@ref s 665(5) The certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act as to re-registration have been complied with (src:8857-8857)
GIVEN `the document is the certificate issued under section 665` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 665(5) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to re-registration have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `the document is the certificate issued under section 665`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The certificate is conclusive evidence": only the certificate of this section

-- ---- s 666: effect of failure to re-register -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:8859 | (1) If a public company that is required by section 662 to apply to be re-registered as a private company fails to do so before the end of the period specified in subsection (3) of that section, Chapter 1 of Part 20 (prohibition of public offers by private company) applies to it as if it were a private company.
@ref s 666(1) Effect of failure to re-register: Chapter 1 of Part 20 applies as if private (src:8859-8859)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is required by section 662 to apply to be re-registered as a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the period specified in section 662(3)` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company applied for re-registration, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 666(1) Chapter 1 of Part 20 applies to the company as if it were a private company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the company is required by section 662 to apply to be re-registered as a private company`
    THEN CONSIDER `the date on which the company applied for re-registration, if it did`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST applied THEN
              IF applied AT MOST `the end of the period specified in section 662(3)`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a public company that is required by section 662 to apply to be re-registered as a private company fails to do so before the end of the period specified in subsection (3) of that section" (an application on the last day is in time: fork F-end)
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a public company that is required by section 662 to apply to be re-registered as a private company fails to do so"

-- src:8860 | (2) Subject to that, the company continues to be treated as a public company until it is so re-registered.
@ref s 666(2) The company continues to be treated as a public company until it is re-registered (src:8860-8860)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been re-registered as a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 666(2) the company continues to be treated as a public company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company continues to be treated as a public company"
    ELSE IF `the company has been re-registered as a private company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until it is so re-registered"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8862 | (1) This section applies where a company, when required to do by section 662—
-- src:8863 | (a) fails to cancel any shares, or
-- src:8864 | (b) fails to make an application for re-registration as a private company,
-- src:8865 | within the time specified in subsection (3) of that section.
-- src:8866 | (2) An offence is committed by—
-- src:8867 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8868 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 667(2) Offence (src:8862-8868)
GIVEN `the company, when required to do so by section 662, fails to cancel any shares or to apply for re-registration within the time specified in section 662(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company, when required to do so by section 662, fails to cancel any shares or to apply for re-registration within the time specified in section 662(3)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company, when required to do by section 662—"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:8869 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 667(3) Penalty (src:8869-8869)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 667(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states the penalty on summary conviction only
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF how, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- ---- s 668: application of provisions to a company re-registering as a public company ------------------

-- src:8871 | (1) This section applies where, after shares in a private company—
-- src:8872 | (a) are forfeited in pursuance of the company's articles or are surrendered to the company in lieu of forfeiture,
-- src:8873 | (b) are acquired by the company (otherwise than by any of the methods permitted by this Part or Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)), the company having a beneficial interest in the shares,
-- src:8874 | (c) are acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance being given directly or indirectly by the company, the company having a beneficial interest in the shares, or
-- src:8875 | (d) are acquired by a person with financial assistance given to him, directly or indirectly, by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition, the company having a beneficial interest in the shares,
-- src:8876 | the company is re-registered as a public company.
@ref s 668(1) Application of provisions to a company re-registering as a public company (src:8871-8876)
DECLARE `s 668(1) how the shares came to be held by or for the private company` IS ONE OF
    `s 668(1)(a) forfeited in pursuance of the company's articles or surrendered to the company in lieu of forfeiture`
    `s 668(1)(b) acquired by the company otherwise than by any method permitted by Part 18 or Part 30`
    `s 668(1)(c) acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance given by the company`
    `s 668(1)(d) acquired by a person with financial assistance given to him by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition`
    `s 668(1) in another way`

DECLARE `s 668(1) shares held by or for a private company` HAS
    `s 668(1) how the shares came to be held` IS A `s 668(1) how the shares came to be held by or for the private company`
    `s 668(1)(b) to (d) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 668(1) the company is re-registered as a public company after that` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 668(1) Application of provisions to a company re-registering as a public company (src:8871-8876)
GIVEN held IS A `s 668(1) shares held by or for a private company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 668(1) this section applies to the shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT held's `s 668(1) the company is re-registered as a public company after that`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where, after shares in a private company— ... the company is re-registered as a public company."
    ELSE CONSIDER held's `s 668(1) how the shares came to be held`
         WHEN `s 668(1)(a) forfeited in pursuance of the company's articles or surrendered to the company in lieu of forfeiture` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 668(1) in another way` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where, after shares in a private company— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..."
         OTHERWISE
              IF held's `s 668(1)(b) to (d) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company having a beneficial interest in the shares"

-- src:8877 | (2) In that case the provisions of sections 662 to 667 apply to the company as if it had been a public company at the time of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition, subject to the following modification.
@ref s 668(2) Sections 662 to 667 apply as if the company had been a public company at the time (src:8877-8877)
GIVEN held IS A `s 668(1) shares held by or for a private company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 668(2) sections 662 to 667 apply to the company as if it had been a public company at the time` MEANS
    `s 668(1) this section applies to the shares` held

-- src:8878 | (3) The modification is that the period specified in section 662(3)(a), (b) or (c) (period for complying with obligations under that section) runs from the date of the re-registration of the company as a public company.
@ref s 668(3) The period in section 662(3) runs from the date of the re-registration of the company as a public company (src:8878-8878)
GIVEN held IS A `s 668(1) shares held by or for a private company`
      `the date of the re-registration of the company as a public company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 668(3) the date from which the period specified in section 662(3) runs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 668(1) this section applies to the shares` held
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the date of the re-registration of the company as a public company`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the following modification": the modification is stated for the company to which section 668 applies

-- ---- s 669: transfer to reserve on acquisition of shares by a public company or nominee -----------------

DECLARE `s 669(2) what the company holds` IS ONE OF
    `s 669(2) shares in the company` HAS `s 669(2) value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
    `s 669(2) an interest in shares in the company` HAS `s 669(2) value to the company of its interest in the shares` IS A NUMBER

-- A rule of reading: "Subsection (1) applies to an interest in shares as it applies to shares. ... the reference to the value of the shares shall be read as a reference to the value to the company of its interest in the shares."
-- src:8884 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to an interest in shares as it applies to shares.
-- src:8885 | As it so applies the reference to the value of the shares shall be read as a reference to the value to the company of its interest in the shares.
@ref s 669(2) Subsection (1) applies to an interest in shares as it applies to shares (src:8884-8885)
GIVEN held IS A `s 669(2) what the company holds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 669(2) the value to read for the purposes of s 669(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER held
    WHEN `s 669(2) shares in the company` v THEN v
    WHEN `s 669(2) an interest in shares in the company` v THEN v

-- src:8880 | (1) Where—
-- src:8881 | (a) a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company, and
-- src:8882 | (b) those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset,
-- src:8883 | an amount equal to the value of the shares must be transferred out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund and is not then available for distribution.
@ref s 669(1) A public company, or its nominee, that acquires shares in the company shown as an asset must transfer an amount to a reserve fund (src:8880-8883)
GIVEN `a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669(1) an amount must be transferred out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund` MEANS
    IF `a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company`
       AND `those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company, and (b) those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset, an amount equal to the value of the shares must be transferred"

-- src:8880 | (1) Where—
-- src:8881 | (a) a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company, and
-- src:8882 | (b) those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset,
-- src:8883 | an amount equal to the value of the shares must be transferred out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund and is not then available for distribution.
-- src:8884 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to an interest in shares as it applies to shares.
-- src:8885 | As it so applies the reference to the value of the shares shall be read as a reference to the value to the company of its interest in the shares.
@ref s 669(1) and (2) The amount to be transferred (src:8880-8885)
GIVEN `a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `s 669(2) what the company holds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 669(1) the amount to be transferred to the reserve fund` MEANS
    IF `a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company`
       AND `those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset`
    THEN `s 669(2) the value to read for the purposes of s 669(1)` held
    ELSE 0 -- no amount is required where the two conditions of subsection (1) are not both met (FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) ... and (b) ...")

@ref s 669(1) The amount transferred is not then available for distribution (src:8880-8883)
GIVEN `a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669(1) the amount transferred is available for distribution` MEANS
    IF `a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquires shares in the company`
       AND `those shares are shown in a balance sheet of the company as an asset`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and is not then available for distribution"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an amount equal to the value of the shares must be transferred out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund and is not then available for distribution": the sentence concerns the amount transferred

@ref s 669(1) The company must transfer an amount equal to the value of the shares to a reserve fund (src:8880-8883)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 661(4) act in Chapter 1`
`s 669(1) the company must transfer an amount to a reserve fund` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 669(1) transfer an amount equal to the value of the shares out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 669(1): no amount equal to the value of the shares was transferred to a reserve fund"

-- ---- s 670: public companies: general rule against lien or charge on own shares -----------------------

-- src:8888 | (1) A lien or other charge of a public company on its own shares (whether taken expressly or otherwise) is void, except as permitted by this section.
-- src:8889 | (2) In the case of any description of company, a charge is permitted if the shares are not fully paid up and the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares.
-- src:8890 | (3) In the case of a company whose ordinary business—
-- src:8891 | (a) includes the lending of money, or
-- src:8892 | (b) consists of the provision of credit or the bailment (in Scotland, hiring) of goods under a hire-purchase agreement, or both,
-- src:8893 | a charge is permitted (whether the shares are fully paid or not) if it arises in connection with a transaction entered into by the company in the ordinary course of that business.
-- src:8894 | (4) In the case of a company that has been re-registered as a public company, a charge is permitted if it was in existence immediately before the application for re-registration.
@ref s 670 Public companies: general rule against lien or charge on own shares (src:8888-8894)
DECLARE `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares` HAS
    `s 670(1) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(2) the shares are not fully paid up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(2) the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(3)(a) the company's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(3)(b) the company's ordinary business consists of the provision of credit or the bailment of goods under a hire-purchase agreement, or both` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(3) the charge arises in connection with a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(4) the company has been re-registered as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 670(4) the charge was in existence immediately before the application for re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 670(2) In the case of any description of company, a charge is permitted if the shares are not fully paid up and the charge is for an amount payable (src:8890-8890)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 670(2) the charge is permitted` MEANS
    IF charge's `s 670(2) the shares are not fully paid up` AND charge's `s 670(2) the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a charge is permitted if the shares are not fully paid up and the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares" (this limb does not permit; another limb may)

@ref s 670(3) A charge is permitted for a company whose ordinary business includes lending or credit, if it arises in the ordinary course (src:8891-8893)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 670(3) the charge is permitted` MEANS
    IF (charge's `s 670(3)(a) the company's ordinary business includes the lending of money`
        OR charge's `s 670(3)(b) the company's ordinary business consists of the provision of credit or the bailment of goods under a hire-purchase agreement, or both`)
       AND charge's `s 670(3) the charge arises in connection with a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a charge is permitted (whether the shares are fully paid or not) if it arises in connection with a transaction entered into by the company in the ordinary course of that business" (this limb does not permit; another limb may)

@ref s 670(4) A company re-registered as a public company: a charge in existence immediately before the application is permitted (src:8894-8894)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 670(4) the charge is permitted` MEANS
    IF charge's `s 670(4) the company has been re-registered as a public company`
       AND charge's `s 670(4) the charge was in existence immediately before the application for re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a charge is permitted if it was in existence immediately before the application for re-registration" (this limb does not permit; another limb may)

@ref s 670(1) A lien or other charge of a public company on its own shares is void, except as permitted (src:8888-8888)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 670(1) the lien or charge is void` MEANS
    IF (NOT charge's `s 670(1) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A lien or other charge of a public company on its own shares"
    ELSE IF (`s 670(2) the charge is permitted` charge) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (`s 670(3) the charge is permitted` charge) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (`s 670(4) the charge is permitted` charge) EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is void, except as permitted by this section"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- ss 671 to 676: supplementary provisions -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:8897 | In determining for the purposes of this Chapter whether a company has a beneficial interest in shares, there shall be disregarded any such interest as is mentioned in—
-- src:8898 | section 672 (residual interest under pension scheme or employees' share scheme),
-- src:8899 | section 673 (employer's charges and other rights of recovery), or
-- src:8900 | section 674 (rights as personal representative or trustee).
@ref s 671 Interests to be disregarded in determining whether the company has a beneficial interest (src:8897-8900)
GIVEN `s 672(1) the residual interest is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 673 the charge, lien, set-off or right is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 674 the right is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 671 the interest is to be disregarded in determining whether the company has a beneficial interest` MEANS
    IF (`s 672(1) the residual interest is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 673 the charge, lien, set-off or right is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 674 the right is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "there shall be disregarded any such interest as is mentioned in section 672, 673 or 674": the section says what is disregarded, not what counts

-- src:8902 | (1) Where the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme, there shall be disregarded any residual interest of the company that has not vested in possession.
@ref s 672(1) Shares held on trust for a pension scheme or employees' share scheme: a residual interest of the company that has not vested in possession is disregarded (src:8902-8902)
GIVEN `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residual interest of the company has vested in possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672(1) the residual interest is to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` AND (NOT `the residual interest of the company has vested in possession`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any residual interest of the company that has not vested in possession"

DECLARE `s 672(2) event` IS ONE OF
    `s 672(2)(a) all the liabilities arising under the scheme having been satisfied or provided for`
    `s 672(2)(b) the company ceasing to participate in the scheme`
    `s 672(2)(c) the trust property at any time exceeding what is necessary for satisfying the liabilities arising or expected to arise under the scheme`
    `s 672(2) any other event`

-- src:8903 | (2) A “residual interest” means a right of the company to receive any of the trust property in the event of—
-- src:8904 | (a) all the liabilities arising under the scheme having been satisfied or provided for, or
-- src:8905 | (b) the company ceasing to participate in the scheme, or
-- src:8906 | (c) the trust property at any time exceeding what is necessary for satisfying the liabilities arising or expected to arise under the scheme.
@ref s 672(2) A residual interest means a right of the company to receive any of the trust property in the event of (a), (b) or (c) (src:8903-8906)
GIVEN `the right is a right of the company to receive any of the trust property` IS A BOOLEAN
      event IS A `s 672(2) event`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672(2) the right is a residual interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `s 672(2) any other event` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “residual interest” means a right of the company to receive any of the trust property in the event of— (a) ... (b) ... (c)"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the right is a right of the company to receive any of the trust property`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “residual interest” means a right of the company to receive any of the trust property"

-- src:8908 | (a) the reference to a right includes a right dependent on the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person, and
@ref s 672(3)(a) The reference to a right includes a right dependent on the exercise of a discretion (src:8908-8908)
GIVEN `the right is dependent on the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672(3)(a) the right is a right within subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the right is dependent on the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to a right includes a right dependent on the exercise of a discretion"

-- src:8909 | (b) the reference to liabilities arising under a scheme includes liabilities that have resulted, or may result, from the exercise of any such discretion.
@ref s 672(3)(b) The reference to liabilities includes liabilities that have resulted, or may result, from the exercise of a discretion (src:8909-8909)
GIVEN `the liability has resulted, or may result, from the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672(3)(b) the liability is a liability arising under the scheme` MEANS
    IF `the liability has resulted, or may result, from the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to liabilities arising under a scheme includes liabilities that have resulted, or may result, from the exercise of any such discretion"

-- src:8910 | (4) For the purposes of this section a residual interest vests in possession—
-- src:8911 | (a) in a case within subsection (2)(a), on the occurrence of the event mentioned there (whether or not the amount of the property receivable pursuant to the right is ascertained);
-- src:8912 | (b) in a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c), when the company becomes entitled to require the trustee to transfer to it any of the property receivable pursuant to that right.
@ref s 672(4) When a residual interest vests in possession (src:8910-8912)
GIVEN event IS A `s 672(2) event`
      `the event mentioned in subsection (2)(a) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has become entitled to require the trustee to transfer to it any of the property receivable pursuant to the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672(4) the residual interest vests in possession` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `s 672(2)(a) all the liabilities arising under the scheme having been satisfied or provided for` THEN
         IF `the event mentioned in subsection (2)(a) has occurred`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (2)(a), on the occurrence of the event mentioned there (whether or not the amount of the property receivable pursuant to the right is ascertained)"
    WHEN `s 672(2)(b) the company ceasing to participate in the scheme` THEN
         IF `the company has become entitled to require the trustee to transfer to it any of the property receivable pursuant to the right`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c), when the company becomes entitled to require the trustee to transfer to it any of the property receivable pursuant to that right"
    WHEN `s 672(2)(c) the trust property at any time exceeding what is necessary for satisfying the liabilities arising or expected to arise under the scheme` THEN
         IF `the company has become entitled to require the trustee to transfer to it any of the property receivable pursuant to the right`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c), when the company becomes entitled to require the trustee to transfer to it any of the property receivable pursuant to that right"
    WHEN `s 672(2) any other event` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) states when a residual interest vests in possession for the three events of subsection (2) only

-- src:8913 | (5) Where by virtue of this section shares are exempt from section 660 or 661 (shares held by company's nominee) at the time they are taken, issued or acquired but the residual interest in question vests in possession before they are disposed of or fully paid up, those sections apply to the shares as if they had been taken, issued or acquired on the date on which that interest vests in possession.
@ref s 672(5) Shares exempt from sections 660 and 661 by virtue of this section: those sections apply from the date the interest vests in possession (src:8913-8913)
GIVEN `by virtue of section 672 the shares are exempt from section 660 or 661 at the time they are taken, issued or acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residual interest vests in possession before the shares are disposed of or fully paid up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the interest vests in possession` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 672(5) the date on which sections 660 and 661 are treated as applying to the shares` MEANS
    IF `by virtue of section 672 the shares are exempt from section 660 or 661 at the time they are taken, issued or acquired`
       AND `the residual interest vests in possession before the shares are disposed of or fully paid up`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the interest vests in possession`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where by virtue of this section shares are exempt from section 660 or 661 ... but the residual interest in question vests in possession before they are disposed of or fully paid up": no date is stated for another case

-- src:8914 | (6) Where by virtue of this section shares are exempt from sections 662 to 668 (shares held by or for public company) at the time they are acquired but the residual interest in question vests in possession before they are disposed of, those sections apply to the shares as if they had been acquired on the date on which the interest vests in possession.
@ref s 672(6) Shares exempt from sections 662 to 668 by virtue of this section: those sections apply from the date the interest vests in possession (src:8914-8914)
GIVEN `by virtue of section 672 the shares are exempt from sections 662 to 668 at the time they are acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residual interest vests in possession before the shares are disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the interest vests in possession` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 672(6) the date on which sections 662 to 668 are treated as applying to the shares` MEANS
    IF `by virtue of section 672 the shares are exempt from sections 662 to 668 at the time they are acquired`
       AND `the residual interest vests in possession before the shares are disposed of`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the interest vests in possession`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where by virtue of this section shares are exempt from sections 662 to 668 ... but the residual interest in question vests in possession before they are disposed of": no date is stated for another case

-- src:8916 | (1) Where the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme there shall be disregarded—
-- src:8917 | (a) any charge or lien on, or set-off against, any benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member;
-- src:8918 | (b) any right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained—
-- src:8919 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:8920 | (ii) under section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 (c. 49), or otherwise, as reimbursement or partial reimbursement for any contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme under Part 3 of that Act.
@ref s 673(1) Pension scheme: a charge, lien or set-off for the employer's monetary obligation is disregarded (src:8916-8920)
GIVEN `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673(1)(a) the charge, lien or set-off is to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme`
       AND `it is a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme there shall be disregarded— (a) any charge or lien on, or set-off against, any benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer"

@ref s 673(1)(b) Pension scheme: a right to receive or retain an amount recoverable under s 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 is disregarded (src:8916-8920)
GIVEN `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained under section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993, or otherwise, as reimbursement of contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673(1)(b) the right is to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme`
       AND `it is a right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained under section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993, or otherwise, as reimbursement of contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) any right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained— (ii) under section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 (c. 49), or otherwise, as reimbursement or partial reimbursement for any contributions equivalent premium paid"

-- src:8921 | (2) Where the shares are held on trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme, there shall be disregarded any charge or lien on, or set-off against, any benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member.
@ref s 673(2) Employees' share scheme: a charge, lien or set-off for the employer's monetary obligation is disregarded (src:8921-8921)
GIVEN `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673(2) the charge, lien or set-off is to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held on trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme`
       AND `it is a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the shares are held on trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme there shall be disregarded any charge or lien on, or set-off against, any benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member"

DECLARE `s 674 right of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 674(a) a right to recover its expenses or be remunerated out of the estate or trust property`
    `s 674(b) a right to be indemnified out of the property for a liability incurred by an act or omission in the performance of its duties`
    `s 674 any other right the company has as personal representative or trustee`
    `s 674 a right the company does not have in that capacity`

-- src:8923 | Where the company is a personal representative or trustee, there shall be disregarded any rights that the company has in that capacity including, in particular—
-- src:8924 | (a) any right to recover its expenses or be remunerated out of the estate or trust property, and
-- src:8925 | (b) any right to be indemnified out of that property for any liability incurred by reason of any act or omission of the company in the performance of its duties as personal representative or trustee.
@ref s 674 Rights as personal representative or trustee (src:8923-8925)
GIVEN `the company is a personal representative or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      right IS A `s 674 right of the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 674 the right is to be disregarded` MEANS
    CONSIDER right
    WHEN `s 674 a right the company does not have in that capacity` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any rights that the company has in that capacity"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the company is a personal representative or trustee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the company is a personal representative or trustee"

-- src:8927 | (1) In this Chapter “pension scheme” means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees.
@ref s 675(1) Pension scheme means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits (src:8927-8927)
GIVEN `it is a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are for or in respect of employees or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(1) the scheme is a pension scheme` MEANS
    IF `it is a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits` AND `the benefits are for or in respect of employees or former employees`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Chapter “pension scheme” means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees."

DECLARE `s 675(2) kind of benefit` IS ONE OF
    `s 675(2) a pension`
    `s 675(2) a lump sum`
    `s 675(2) a gratuity`
    `s 675(2) another like benefit`
    `s 675(2) a benefit of another kind`

DECLARE `s 675(2) occasion on which the benefit is given` IS ONE OF
    `s 675(2) on retirement`
    `s 675(2) on death`
    `s 675(2) in anticipation of retirement`
    `s 675(2) in connection with past service, after retirement or death`
    `s 675(2) on another occasion`

-- src:8928 | (2) In subsection (1) “relevant benefits” means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or, in connection with past service, after retirement or death.
@ref s 675(2) Relevant benefits means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or in connection with past service (src:8928-8928)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 675(2) kind of benefit`
      occasion IS A `s 675(2) occasion on which the benefit is given`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(2) the benefit is a relevant benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 675(2) a benefit of another kind` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant benefits” means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER occasion
        WHEN `s 675(2) on another occasion` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or, in connection with past service, after retirement or death"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8930 | For the purposes of this Chapter references to “employer” and “employee”, in the context of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme, shall be read as if a director of a company were employed by it.
@ref s 676 Application of provisions to directors: a director is read as employed by the company (src:8930-8930)
GIVEN `the reference is to an employer or employee in the context of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 676 the director is treated as employed by the company` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to an employer or employee in the context of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` AND `the person is a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "references to “employer” and “employee”, in the context of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme, shall be read as if a director of a company were employed by it"
